## Adding a new reference (`download-ref` skill)

`download-ref` is the entry point for any "add this arXiv/DOI to the KB" request. It is provided by the `zlp-harness` plugin and resolves its bundled helper scripts from the plugin skill directory:

1. `fetch_metadata.py --kb .knowledge --manifest <json> --download-arxiv-pdfs`
2. `render.py --kb .knowledge` (uses `pymupdf4llm` if available — preserves figures; falls back to `markitdown` then `pdftotext`)
3. `index.py --kb .knowledge --title "<<TOPIC>> — references" --source-note "Reading list and full-text harness for the <<TOPIC>> project. arXiv preprints, DOIs (with arXiv-preprint fallbacks where the publisher gates the PDF)."`

Invariants the skill assumes:
- The renderer needs `pymupdf4llm` available to whichever Python `python3` resolves to. Installing it into a different Python environment will not satisfy the helper — run `python3 -c "import sys; print(sys.executable)"` first.
- `--source-note` and `--title` strings must stay stable across runs or `INDEX.md` will churn. Copy them verbatim from the existing `INDEX.md` header on every re-run.

When `download-ref` finishes, **do not** auto-append to `ref.bib` unless this repo has a LaTeX draft (`main.tex`) — the append step in the skill is dormant until then.

## Zulip channel — discussion archive

Co-author chat lives in the **`<<ZULIP_STREAM>>`** stream on <<ZULIP_SITE>>. The `Makefile` at the repo root wraps the [`zlp`](https://pypi.org/project/zlp-cli/) CLI to mirror that stream into the global workspace directory printed by `make zulip-config` (one folder per Zulip workspace, shared across every harness on the same workspace).

The Makefile pins the stream and exports the env vars `zlp` needs (`ZULIP_CONFIG_FILE`, `ZLP_ARCHIVE_ROOT`, `ZLP_RUN_ROOT`) — all of them point inside the workspace dir. On a fresh clone the workspace dir does not exist yet; `/onboard` creates it after the user downloads `zuliprc`. If `zlp` isn't installed: `pip install zlp-cli`. Commands are listed in the "Common commands" section above.

Caveats / gotchas:
- Stream-wide pulls land in a hash-suffixed folder like `_all-<hash>/` (a `zlp` slugify quirk for the placeholder topic name). Topic-narrowed pulls produce the cleaner `<topic-slug>/` folder.
- `make zulip-pull` mirrors the **user's own outgoing messages** as `.md` files too. Filter by `make zulip-whoami` display name when summarizing co-author traffic.
- `make zulip-send` silently creates a new topic if `TOPIC=` doesn't match an existing one (case- and whitespace-sensitive). Verify with `make zulip-topics | grep -F "<topic>"` before sending.
- Drafts being staged for `MSG_FILE=` should be written under `$(ZULIP_DRAFTS_DIR)` (the workspace's `.drafts/` subdir), never inside the repo. Use `make zulip-config` to read the path.
- Never add an AI-attribution signature to outgoing Zulip messages. The account name is the only attribution.

## Doing common tasks

**"What's the latest on <subtopic>?"** → `rg "<keyword>" .knowledge/` first; then read the matched `.md` files.

**"Add this arXiv ref"** → Use the `download-ref` skill. Manifest accepts both `arxiv` and `doi` lists; the skill is idempotent.

**"Post links to Zulip"** → Draft to `$(ZULIP_DRAFTS_DIR)/<file>.md` (workspace dir; read it via `make zulip-config`), then `make zulip-send TOPIC="<topic>" MSG_FILE="$(ZULIP_DRAFTS_DIR)/<file>.md"`. Match the existing message style in the target topic (concise, numbered, `[Title](URL)`); check with `make zulip-messages TOPIC="<topic>" LIMIT=5` first.

**"Check Zulip" / "what did X say" / "draft a reply"** → invoke the **`zulip-reply` skill** from the plugin. It pulls new messages, grounds each in `.knowledge/`, walks them one-by-one with quoted-body context, and asks before sending.

**"Weekly advisor check" / "student TODOs" / "latest updates for the project"** → invoke the **`zlp-advisor` skill** from the plugin. It reviews the last week of Zulip discussion, checks that student TODOs are created and respected, searches reliable current sources, and drafts a weekly advisor post for approval.

